%[text] %[text:anchor:H_330E72C3] ### Getting Started
%[text] #### Accessing the Module
%[text] #### **On MATLAB Online:**
%[text] Use the [![Open in MATLAB Online Button](text:image:3ed8)](https://matlab.mathworks.com/open/github/v1?repo=MathWorks-Teaching-Resources/Matrix-Methods-of-Linear-Algebra&project=MatrixMethods.prj) link to download the module. You will be prompted to log in or create a MathWorks account. The project will be loaded, and you will see an app with several navigation options to get you started.
%[text] #### **On Desktop:**
%[text] Download or clone this repository. Open MATLAB, navigate to the folder containing these scripts and double-click on [MatrixMethods.prj](<matlab: openProject("MatrixMethods.prj")>). It will add the appropriate files to your MATLAB path and open an app that asks you where you would like to start. 
%[text] Ensure you have all the required products ([listed below](internal:H_E850B4FF)) installed. If you need to include a product, add it using the Add-On Explorer. To install an add-on, go to the **Home** tab and select  ![Add-ons icon](text:image:5a12) **Add-Ons** \> **Get Add-Ons**. 
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E850B4FF] ### Products
%[text] MATLAB® is used throughout. Tools from Symbolic Math Toolbox™, Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox™, and Image Processing Toolbox™ are used as well.
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E8C62B23] ## Scripts
%[text] ### [MatrixOperations.m](file:./Scripts/MatrixOperations.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,682,308],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Rhino with pixel values](text:image:83cd) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Define matrices and their basic arithmetic operations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Calculate the result of matrix operations on paper and in MATLAB</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Explain the size requirements of matrix operations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Compare symbolic and numeric matrix operations in MATLAB</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Apply matrix methods to modify grayscale images</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Linear algebra</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Image processing</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [LinearSystems.m](file:./Scripts/LinearSystems.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,682,308],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![3-D linear system](text:image:7fc2) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Write a linear system in matrix form</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Relate solutions of linear systems in 3-dimensions to their visualizations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Solve systems of linear equations using row-reduction and matrix inverses</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Explain the solvability of a linear system in terms of the matrix determinant</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Use MATLAB to solve linear systems</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Linear algebra</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [LinearSystemsApplications.m](file:./Scripts/LinearSystemsApplications.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,683,308],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Linear regression and circuit analysis](text:image:26f8) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Apply matrix methods to linear regression and linear circuit analysis</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Linear algebra</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Statistical analysis</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Circuit analysis</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [Eigenanalysis.m](file:./Scripts/Eigenanalysis.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,683,308],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Eigenvector in 2-D](text:image:4ff2) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Visualize eigenvectors in 2-dimensions</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Solve for the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a 2x2 matrix on paper and larger matrices using MATLAB</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Diagonalize 2x2 matrices on paper and larger matrices in MATLAB</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Explain linear system solvability in terms of eigenvalues</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"}Discuss defective matrices</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Linear algebra</p> |
%[text] | --- | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] ### [EigenanalysisApplications.m](file:./Scripts/EigenanalysisApplications.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,682,308],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Markov chain visualization](text:image:879c) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Use eigenanalysis to understand vibrations and the long term behavior of a Markov chain</p><p></p> | <p>**Academic disciplines**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Linear algebra</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Physical systems</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} Statistical modeling</p> |
